Problem: People who regularly buy and store groceries at home often forget about 
items that are approaching their expiration dates. As a result, food may expire before it is used, causing 
unnecessary food waste and money loss. 

Who exactly has it:   Parents, working adults, and people who regularly purchase and store 
groceries for themselves or their household. 

Why it matters / what it costs them today:  They may waste money by throwing away expired food and 
spend extra time manually checking expiration dates, and having problems after eating expired food.  
